# Decode-round timing tables (TF_GLM_EST, on by default): how many milliseconds a verify forward over R rows takes
# on the GPU (a CUDA event pair, read after the round's sampler has synchronized it anyway) and how long the
# sampler's host side takes, sliding medians per verify-row count, from DeepInfer's ForwardRuntimeEstimator /
# SamplerRuntimeEstimator pattern (its MTPVarlen confidence-scheduled verification reads exactly these two tables).
# Read-only observation on both ranks: nothing branches on it yet, so the ranks stay in step; a verify-budget
# search will be the first reader. New tensorfold/families/glm5_next/cuda/estimators.py, hooks in the multi-stream
# round, /health's "est" and /metrics's tensorfold_health:est_* gauges.
